BT /F1 16 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 720 Tm (Field Guide to Urban Beekeeping) Tj /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 700 Tm (A practical handbook for small-apiary managers.) Tj /F1 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 664 Tm (Chapter 1: Colony Structure) Tj /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 646 Tm (A healthy hive in midsummer can contain up to 60,000 worker bees,) Tj /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 630 Tm (plus one queen and a few hundred drones depending on the season.) Tj /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 614 Tm (The queen lays up to 2,000 eggs per day at the peak of spring buildup.) Tj /F1 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 578 Tm (Chapter 2: Equipment) Tj /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 560 Tm (The Langstroth hive uses removable frames and relies on the bee space:) Tj /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 544 Tm (a corridor of 6 to 9 millimeters that bees keep free of comb and propolis.) Tj /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 528 Tm (Smokers calm bees by masking alarm pheromones during inspections.) Tj /F1 13 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 492 Tm (Chapter 3: Hive Products) Tj /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 474 Tm (Propolis is a resinous substance bees collect from plant buds and use) Tj /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 458 Tm (to seal small gaps and sterilize the interior of the hive.) Tj /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 442 Tm (Honey is harvested only when its moisture content drops below 18 percent,) Tj /F1 11 Tf 1 0 0 1 60 426 Tm (which prevents fermentation during storage.) Tj ET
